  "notes": "{煮|に}える describes food reaching a state of being fully cooked in boiling liquid.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {煮|に}る (transitive, to cook/boil something)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{煮|に}えている means 'is cooked/done' (resulting state). Example: {野菜|やさい}が{煮|に}えている (the vegetables are cooked).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {野菜|やさい}が{煮|に}える: vegetables get cooked\n- よく{煮|に}える: to cook thoroughly\n- まだ{煮|に}えていない: not cooked yet\n\nIDIOMS:\n- {煮|に}ても{焼|や}いても{食|く}えない: someone impossible to deal with (lit. 'can't eat whether boiled or grilled')\n- {業|ごう}を{煮|に}やす: to lose patience",
